"'Diligence is said to be the best of them' (1.1). Needs a pattern for ranking." owl:sameAs "'Diligence is said to be the best of them' (1.1). Needs a pattern for ranking." .

"'Rational application of mind is said to be the best of them' (1.1). Needs a pattern for ranking." owl:sameAs "'Rational application of mind is said to be the best of them' (1.1). Needs a pattern for ranking." .

"0.1" owl:sameAs "0.1" .

"All 24 statements of what fuels and starves the five hindrances and seven awakening factors, each as a nutriment node (object + kind of attention + effect). The opening statement (1.2) anchors both lists." owl:sameAs "All 24 statements of what fuels and starves the five hindrances and seven awakening factors, each as a nutriment node (object + kind of attention + effect). The opening statement (1.2) anchors both lists." .

"All ascetics and brahmins, past, future and present, who give up the three discriminations do so by developing the seven factors (1.2-1.4, 1.7-1.9); the list (1.6). The sutta doesn't name the three discriminations, so neither does the ontology." owl:sameAs "All ascetics and brahmins, past, future and present, who give up the three discriminations do so by developing the seven factors (1.2-1.4, 1.7-1.9); the list (1.6). The sutta doesn't name the three discriminations, so neither does the ontology." .

"As they are developed the mind is freed from the defilements of sensuality, desire to be reborn and ignorance, and knows it is freed (1.8-1.10). Needs the three defilements (āsava) as a list and a pattern for release." owl:sameAs "As they are developed the mind is freed from the defilements of sensuality, desire to be reborn and ignorance, and knows it is freed (1.8-1.10). Needs the three defilements (āsava) as a list and a pattern for release." .

"As they investigate principles with wisdom in this way their energy is roused up and unflagging" owl:sameAs "As they investigate principles with wisdom in this way their energy is roused up and unflagging" .

"As they live mindfully in this way they investigate, explore, and inquire into that teaching with wisdom" owl:sameAs "As they live mindfully in this way they investigate, explore, and inquire into that teaching with wisdom" .

"Both lists (1.1, 1.3-1.7; 2.1, 2.3); the hindrances weaken wisdom (1.1, 1.8); developing the awakening factors leads to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom (2.1, 2.4)." owl:sameAs "Both lists (1.1, 1.3-1.7; 2.1, 2.3); the hindrances weaken wisdom (1.1, 1.8); developing the awakening factors leads to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom (2.1, 2.4)." .

"Both lists (1.1, 1.3; 2.1, 2.3); the hindrances block wisdom and don't lead to extinguishment (1.1, 1.8); the awakening factors grow wisdom and lead to extinguishment (2.1, 2.4)." owl:sameAs "Both lists (1.1, 1.3; 2.1, 2.3); the hindrances block wisdom and don't lead to extinguishment (1.1, 1.8); the awakening factors grow wisdom and lead to extinguishment (2.1, 2.4)." .

"Both lists (2.1, 2.2; 3.1, 3.2), and the teaching: when a noble disciple pays attention, applies the mind, concentrates wholeheartedly and actively listens to the teaching, the five hindrances are absent and the seven awakening factors are fully developed (1.1, 3.4)." owl:sameAs "Both lists (2.1, 2.2; 3.1, 3.2), and the teaching: when a noble disciple pays attention, applies the mind, concentrates wholeheartedly and actively listens to the teaching, the five hindrances are absent and the seven awakening factors are fully developed (1.1, 3.4)." .

"Developing the seven factors brings one who practices them to the complete ending of suffering (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." owl:sameAs "Developing the seven factors brings one who practices them to the complete ending of suffering (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." .

"Developing the seven factors leads solely to disillusionment, dispassion, cessation, peace, insight, awakening (sambodhi) and extinguishment (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." owl:sameAs "Developing the seven factors leads solely to disillusionment, dispassion, cessation, peace, insight, awakening (sambodhi) and extinguishment (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." .

"Developing the seven factors leads to going from the near shore to the far shore (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." owl:sameAs "Developing the seven factors leads to going from the near shore to the far shore (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." .

"Developing the seven factors leads to growth and progress (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." owl:sameAs "Developing the seven factors leads to growth and progress (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." .

"Developing the seven factors leads to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." owl:sameAs "Developing the seven factors leads to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." .

"Developing the seven factors slants, slopes and inclines to extinguishment (1.2, 2.4); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." owl:sameAs "Developing the seven factors slants, slopes and inclines to extinguishment (1.2, 2.4); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." .

"Everything else. The text is not held; the pairings need checking against an edition before they can be marked verified." owl:sameAs "Everything else. The text is not held; the pairings need checking against an edition before they can be marked verified." .

"Five pairings of a jhāna factor against a hindrance (citing the Peṭakopadesa)." owl:sameAs "Five pairings of a jhāna factor against a hindrance (citing the Peṭakopadesa)." .

"Good friendship is the forerunner of the arising of the seven factors (1.2), and one with good friends can expect to develop them (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (1.6). Same statements as SN 46.12, added as citations." owl:sameAs "Good friendship is the forerunner of the arising of the seven factors (1.2), and one with good friends can expect to develop them (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (1.6). Same statements as SN 46.12, added as citations." .

"Good friendship is the forerunner of the arising of the seven factors (1.2), and one with good friends can expect to develop them (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." owl:sameAs "Good friendship is the forerunner of the arising of the seven factors (1.2), and one with good friends can expect to develop them (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." .

"Irrational application of mind: the hindrances arise and grow (1.1). Rational application of mind: the awakening factors arise and are fully developed (2.1)." owl:sameAs "Irrational application of mind: the hindrances arise and grow (1.1). Rational application of mind: the awakening factors arise and are fully developed (2.1)." .

"Irrational application of mind: the hindrances arise and grow, the awakening factors don't arise or cease (1.1-1.6). Rational application of mind: the hindrances don't arise or are given up, the awakening factors arise and are fully developed (2.1-3.1)." owl:sameAs "Irrational application of mind: the hindrances arise and grow, the awakening factors don't arise or cease (1.1-1.6). Rational application of mind: the hindrances don't arise or are given up, the awakening factors arise and are fully developed (2.1-3.1)." .

"Its 12 statements of what fuels the five hindrances and seven awakening factors (2-6, 9-15). They match SN 46.51 sections 1-12 (identical English; Pali differs only in punctuation and one spelling variant), so they were added as a second citation on the same claims, not as new claims." owl:sameAs "Its 12 statements of what fuels the five hindrances and seven awakening factors (2-6, 9-15). They match SN 46.51 sections 1-12 (identical English; Pali differs only in punctuation and one spelling variant), so they were added as a second citation on the same claims, not as new claims." .

"Its whole teaching: the list of the seven awakening factors (1.1, 1.3, 1.4), as citations on the existing list." owl:sameAs "Its whole teaching: the list of the seven awakening factors (1.1, 1.3, 1.4), as citations on the existing list." .

"Most of the dialogue: wisdom and consciousness (2-6), feeling and perception (7-11), the goal of wisdom and conditions for right view (12-14), states of existence (15-17), what the first absorption is (18), the five faculties (21-22), vital forces and death vs cessation (23-25), and the releases of the heart (26-37)." owl:sameAs "Most of the dialogue: wisdom and consciousness (2-6), feeling and perception (7-11), the goal of wisdom and conditions for right view (12-14), states of existence (15-17), what the first absorption is (18), the five faculties (21-22), vital forces and death vs cessation (23-25), and the releases of the heart (26-37)." .

"Nothing doctrinal. The question (x.1) and conclusion (x.4) of each section restate the claim and are not cited separately." owl:sameAs "Nothing doctrinal. The question (x.1) and conclusion (x.4) of each section restate the claim and are not cited separately." .

"Nothing else, developed like this, leads to giving up the things that tighten the fetters like the seven factors (1.1, 2.3); the list (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.2)." owl:sameAs "Nothing else, developed like this, leads to giving up the things that tighten the fetters like the seven factors (1.1, 2.3); the list (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.2)." .

"Of exterior factors, nothing gives rise to the seven awakening factors like good friendship (1.1). The rest of the sutta is abbreviated in the source." owl:sameAs "Of exterior factors, nothing gives rise to the seven awakening factors like good friendship (1.1). The rest of the sutta is abbreviated in the source." .

"Of interior factors, nothing gives rise to the seven awakening factors like rational application of mind (1.1). The rest of the sutta is abbreviated in the source." owl:sameAs "Of interior factors, nothing gives rise to the seven awakening factors like rational application of mind (1.1). The rest of the sutta is abbreviated in the source." .

"One definition: 'Unification of the mind is immersion' (12.2). Found while checking an eval answer; it corrected decision D4, which had wrongly called this equation an interpretation." owl:sameAs "One definition: 'Unification of the mind is immersion' (12.2). Found while checking an eval answer; it corrected decision D4, which had wrongly called this equation an interpretation." .

"One segment (10.2) as evidence for 'dhamma' meaning the Buddha's teaching." owl:sameAs "One segment (10.2) as evidence for 'dhamma' meaning the Buddha's teaching." .

"One segment (36.2), recorded as a contested use of the word 'dhamma' and deliberately left without a sense." owl:sameAs "One segment (36.2), recorded as a contested use of the word 'dhamma' and deliberately left without a sense." .

"Only the first absorption: its five factors (19.2-19.3), and that it gives up the five hindrances and possesses those five factors (20.2-20.4)." owl:sameAs "Only the first absorption: its five factors (19.2-19.3), and that it gives up the five hindrances and possesses those five factors (20.2-20.4)." .

"Rational application of mind is the forerunner of the arising of the seven factors (1.2), and one accomplished in it can expect to develop them (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." owl:sameAs "Rational application of mind is the forerunner of the arising of the seven factors (1.2), and one accomplished in it can expect to develop them (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." .

"Skillful qualities are rooted in diligence (1.1); a diligent mendicant can expect to develop the seven factors (1.2); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." owl:sameAs "Skillful qualities are rooted in diligence (1.1); a diligent mendicant can expect to develop the seven factors (1.2); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." .

"Skillful qualities are rooted in rational application of mind (1.1); one accomplished in it can expect to develop the seven factors (1.2); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." owl:sameAs "Skillful qualities are rooted in rational application of mind (1.1); one accomplished in it can expect to develop the seven factors (1.2); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." .

"That the factors are 'noble and emancipating' (ariyā niyyānikā) (1.1, 1.4). Needs a pattern for what a quality is called." owl:sameAs "That the factors are 'noble and emancipating' (ariyā niyyānikā) (1.1, 1.4). Needs a pattern for what a quality is called." .

"That the factors are not obstacles, hindrances or corruptions of the mind (1.1, 1.4). Needs a pattern for what a quality is or is not." owl:sameAs "That the factors are not obstacles, hindrances or corruptions of the mind (1.1, 1.4). Needs a pattern for what a quality is or is not." .

"That the hindrances are obstacles and corruptions of the heart, and the awakening factors are not (1.1, 1.8, 2.1, 2.4). Needs a pattern for what a quality is or is not." owl:sameAs "That the hindrances are obstacles and corruptions of the heart, and the awakening factors are not (1.1, 1.8, 2.1, 2.4). Needs a pattern for what a quality is or is not." .

"The Pali compounds 'making blind, sightless, ignorant' and 'on the side of distress' for the hindrances, and their opposites for the awakening factors (1.1, 2.1), which don't map cleanly onto a target concept; and the chapter's summary verse (3.0-3.4)." owl:sameAs "The Pali compounds 'making blind, sightless, ignorant' and 'on the side of distress' for the hindrances, and their opposites for the awakening factors (1.1, 2.1), which don't map cleanly onto a target concept; and the chapter's summary verse (3.0-3.4)." .

"The awakening factors arising in sequence, each step a condition with its own words: recollecting and thinking about the teaching gives rise to mindfulness, then investigation, energy, rapture (not of the flesh), tranquility, immersion (with bliss) and equanimity (1.9-8.1); and the seven fruits and benefits they lead to, from enlightenment early in this life to heading upstream to the Akaniṭṭha realm (9.1-9.10)." owl:sameAs "The awakening factors arising in sequence, each step a condition with its own words: recollecting and thinking about the teaching gives rise to mindfulness, then investigation, energy, rapture (not of the flesh), tranquility, immersion (with bliss) and equanimity (1.9-8.1); and the seven fruits and benefits they lead to, from enlightenment early in this life to heading upstream to the Akaniṭṭha realm (9.1-9.10)." .

"The banner simile and the recollection of the Buddha, the teaching and the Saṅgha as a remedy for fear." owl:sameAs "The banner simile and the recollection of the Buddha, the teaching and the Saṅgha as a remedy for fear." .

"The chain: as they develop each factor, craving is given up; when craving is given up, deeds are given up; when deeds are given up, suffering is given up (2.2-2.4, 2.6-2.9). Needs a pattern for chains of ending, which dependent origination will also need. Also the description of each factor as 'abundant, expansive, limitless, and free of ill will' (2.1, 2.5)." owl:sameAs "The chain: as they develop each factor, craving is given up; when craving is given up, deeds are given up; when deeds are given up, suffering is given up (2.2-2.4, 2.6-2.9). Needs a pattern for chains of ending, which dependent origination will also need. Also the description of each factor as 'abundant, expansive, limitless, and free of ill will' (2.1, 2.5)." .

"The first line of the verse ('All things are not-self') as evidence for 'dhamma' meaning any phenomenon." owl:sameAs "The first line of the verse ('All things are not-self') as evidence for 'dhamma' meaning any phenomenon." .

"The five corruptions of the mind as a list whose members are the same five qualities as the hindrances (2.1, 2.3, 2.4)." owl:sameAs "The five corruptions of the mind as a list whose members are the same five qualities as the hindrances (2.1, 2.3, 2.4)." .

"The five higher fetters as a list (1.2, 1.4); the seven factors should be developed for their direct knowledge, complete understanding, finishing and giving up (1.6, 1.12); and the formula variants: culminating in the removal of greed, hate and delusion (1.9), having freedom from death as their culmination (1.10), and inclining to extinguishment (1.11). The rest of the sutta is abbreviated in the source." owl:sameAs "The five higher fetters as a list (1.2, 1.4); the seven factors should be developed for their direct knowledge, complete understanding, finishing and giving up (1.6, 1.12); and the formula variants: culminating in the removal of greed, hate and delusion (1.9), having freedom from death as their culmination (1.10), and inclining to extinguishment (1.11). The rest of the sutta is abbreviated in the source." .

"The framing: Pūraṇa Kassapa's view that knowing and not knowing have no cause (1.4-1.13). The naming 'these are called the hindrances / awakening factors' (4.2, 7.2). Prince Abhaya's responses, including 'overcome by even a single hindrance you wouldn't truly know or see' and 'endowed with even a single awakening factor you would' (4.3-4.5, 7.3-7.6): said by the interlocutor, not taught, so not encoded (D17)." owl:sameAs "The framing: Pūraṇa Kassapa's view that knowing and not knowing have no cause (1.4-1.13). The naming 'these are called the hindrances / awakening factors' (4.2, 7.2). Prince Abhaya's responses, including 'overcome by even a single hindrance you wouldn't truly know or see' and 'endowed with even a single awakening factor you would' (4.3-4.5, 7.3-7.6): said by the interlocutor, not taught, so not encoded (D17)." .

"The hindrances are a cause and reason for not knowing and not seeing, when the heart is overcome by them (2.3-3.5); the awakening factors are a cause and reason for knowing and seeing (5.3-6.4); the stock formula (5.3, 6.2)." owl:sameAs "The hindrances are a cause and reason for not knowing and not seeing, when the heart is overcome by them (2.3-3.5); the awakening factors are a cause and reason for knowing and seeing (5.3-6.4); the stock formula (5.3, 6.2)." .

"The list of the seven awakening factors (1.7)." owl:sameAs "The list of the seven awakening factors (1.7)." .

"The naming: the seven awakening factors are 'the seven principles that prevent decline' (aparihāniyā dhammā) (1.1, 1.3, 1.5, 1.8). Needs a pattern for what a quality is called." owl:sameAs "The naming: the seven awakening factors are 'the seven principles that prevent decline' (aparihāniyā dhammā) (1.1, 1.3, 1.5, 1.8). Needs a pattern for what a quality is called." .

"The one line given: compassion (Pali: karuṇā), developed and cultivated, is very fruitful and beneficial (1.1)." owl:sameAs "The one line given: compassion (Pali: karuṇā), developed and cultivated, is very fruitful and beneficial (1.1)." .

