"The perception of a skeleton is very fruitful and beneficial (1.2, 1.6), developed together with the awakening factors (1.4), with the stock formula (1.5); one of two results, enlightenment in this very life or non-return; great benefit, great sanctuary from the yoke, great inspiration and great ease." owl:sameAs "The perception of a skeleton is very fruitful and beneficial (1.2, 1.6), developed together with the awakening factors (1.4), with the stock formula (1.5); one of two results, enlightenment in this very life or non-return; great benefit, great sanctuary from the yoke, great inspiration and great ease." .

"The perception of cessation is very fruitful and beneficial (1.2, 1.6), developed together with the awakening factors (1.4), with the stock formula (1.5); one of two results, enlightenment in this very life or non-return; great benefit, great sanctuary from the yoke, great inspiration and great ease." owl:sameAs "The perception of cessation is very fruitful and beneficial (1.2, 1.6), developed together with the awakening factors (1.4), with the stock formula (1.5); one of two results, enlightenment in this very life or non-return; great benefit, great sanctuary from the yoke, great inspiration and great ease." .

"The rest of Dhammadinnā's answers: substantial reality, its origin, cessation and the practice leading there (2-5); grasping and the aggregates (6); substantialist view (7-8); the noble eightfold path and the three spectrums of practice (9-11); the bases, prerequisites and development of immersion (12.3-12.5); the three processes (13-15); the cessation of perception and feeling (16-21); the three feelings, their underlying tendencies and their counterparts (22-29)." owl:sameAs "The rest of Dhammadinnā's answers: substantial reality, its origin, cessation and the practice leading there (2-5); grasping and the aggregates (6); substantialist view (7-8); the noble eightfold path and the three spectrums of practice (9-11); the bases, prerequisites and development of immersion (12.3-12.5); the three processes (13-15); the cessation of perception and feeling (16-21); the three feelings, their underlying tendencies and their counterparts (22-29)." .

"The rest of the verse, and the rest of the Path chapter (Dhp 273-289)." owl:sameAs "The rest of the verse, and the rest of the Path chapter (Dhp 273-289)." .

"The setting and the challenge from wanderers of other religions (1.1-3.1); the four fire similes (5, 8, 11, 14) that illustrate the advice; the repeated statements after each simile (6, 9, 12, 15.1-15.3)." owl:sameAs "The setting and the challenge from wanderers of other religions (1.1-3.1); the four fire similes (5, 8, 11, 14) that illustrate the advice; the repeated statements after each simile (6, 9, 12, 15.1-15.3)." .

"The seven factors are the path for crushing Māra's army (1.1, 1.5, 1.8); the list (1.7)." owl:sameAs "The seven factors are the path for crushing Māra's army (1.1, 1.5, 1.8); the list (1.7)." .

"The seven factors are the path that helps penetration (1.1, 1.5, 1.9, 2.9); the list (1.7); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.1, 2.5)." owl:sameAs "The seven factors are the path that helps penetration (1.1, 1.5, 1.9, 2.9); the list (1.7); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.1, 2.5)." .

"The seven factors are the path that leads to the cessation of craving (1.1, 1.4, 2.3); the list (1.6); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.2)." owl:sameAs "The seven factors are the path that leads to the cessation of craving (1.1, 1.4, 2.3); the list (1.6); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.2)." .

"The seven factors are the path that leads to the ending of craving (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.6); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.1, 2.5)." owl:sameAs "The seven factors are the path that leads to the ending of craving (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.6); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.1, 2.5)." .

"The seven factors developed depending on and grounded on ethics (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." owl:sameAs "The seven factors developed depending on and grounded on ethics (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." .

"The seven factors developed depending on and grounded on ethics (1.4), and the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (1.6, 1.12)." owl:sameAs "The seven factors developed depending on and grounded on ethics (1.4), and the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (1.6, 1.12)." .

"The simile framing the teaching: as the body is sustained by food, so the hindrances and the awakening factors are sustained by fuel (1.2-1.3, 7, 8, 16). There is no pattern for similes yet." owl:sameAs "The simile framing the teaching: as the body is sustained by food, so the hindrances and the awakening factors are sustained by fuel (1.2-1.3, 7, 8, 16). There is no pattern for similes yet." .

"The simile of a bungalow's rafters inclining to the peak (1.1)." owl:sameAs "The simile of a bungalow's rafters inclining to the peak (1.1)." .

"The simile of creatures in the four postures depending on the earth (1.1-1.2)." owl:sameAs "The simile of creatures in the four postures depending on the earth (1.1-1.2)." .

"The simile of dragons growing strong on the Himalayas and reaching the ocean (1.2-1.3), and the result 'acquiring great and abundant good qualities' (1.4, 1.13). No simile pattern yet." owl:sameAs "The simile of dragons growing strong on the Himalayas and reaching the ocean (1.2-1.3), and the result 'acquiring great and abundant good qualities' (1.4, 1.13). No simile pattern yet." .

"The simile of the dawn as forerunner of the sunrise (1.1)." owl:sameAs "The simile of the dawn as forerunner of the sunrise (1.1)." .

"The simile of the five corruptions of native gold (1.1-1.8), and what the corruptions do: the mind is not pliable, workable or radiant, is brittle, and is not rightly immersed for the ending of defilements (2.1, 2.4). No pattern yet for similes or for what a quality does." owl:sameAs "The simile of the five corruptions of native gold (1.1-1.8), and what the corruptions do: the mind is not pliable, workable or radiant, is brittle, and is not rightly immersed for the ending of defilements (2.1, 2.4). No pattern yet for similes or for what a quality does." .

"The six sets of six (sense fields, objects, consciousnesses, contacts, feelings, cravings) and the not-self argument built on them." owl:sameAs "The six sets of six (sense fields, objects, consciousnesses, contacts, feelings, cravings) and the not-self argument built on them." .

"The timing advice: which awakening factors it is the right or wrong time to develop when the mind is sluggish (4.1, 7.1) or restless (10.1, 13.1), the reason given for each, and 'mindfulness is always useful' (15.4)." owl:sameAs "The timing advice: which awakening factors it is the right or wrong time to develop when the mind is sluggish (4.1, 7.1) or restless (10.1, 13.1), the reason given for each, and 'mindfulness is always useful' (15.4)." .

"The verses (2.1-6.6): few cross to the far shore, the astute develop the bright, and those rightly developed in the awakening factors are quenched in this world." owl:sameAs "The verses (2.1-6.6): few cross to the far shore, the astute develop the bright, and those rightly developed in the awakening factors are quenched in this world." .

"The whole teaching on the four kinds of mindfulness meditation. Its section on the five hindrances (knowing when each is present, how it arises, how it is given up) bears directly on this ontology and should come next." owl:sameAs "The whole teaching on the four kinds of mindfulness meditation. Its section on the five hindrances (knowing when each is present, how it arises, how it is given up) bears directly on this ontology and should come next." .

"They closely watch over that mind immersed in samādhi" owl:sameAs "They closely watch over that mind immersed in samādhi" .

"Two segments (5.3, 6.8) as evidence for 'dhamma' meaning an object of the mind." owl:sameAs "Two segments (5.3, 6.8) as evidence for 'dhamma' meaning an object of the mind." .

"What the things that tighten the fetters are: the eye, ear, nose, tongue, body and mind, where the fetters, shackles and attachments arise (3.1-3.8). Needs the six sense fields as a list and a pattern for 'X is where Y arises'." owl:sameAs "What the things that tighten the fetters are: the eye, ear, nose, tongue, body and mind, where the fetters, shackles and attachments arise (3.1-3.8). Needs the six sense fields as a list and a pattern for 'X is where Y arises'." .

"When the body is tranquil and one feels bliss, the mind becomes immersed in samādhi" owl:sameAs "When the body is tranquil and one feels bliss, the mind becomes immersed in samādhi" .

"When the mind is full of rapture, the body and mind become tranquil" owl:sameAs "When the mind is full of rapture, the body and mind become tranquil" .

"Why it matters to see, hear, approach, pay homage to, recollect and go forth following mendicants accomplished in ethics, immersion, knowledge and freedom: 'very helpful' (1.1-1.6); and living withdrawn in body and mind after hearing their teaching (1.8). Needs a pattern for what is called helpful, and the link from hearing to withdrawal is not modelled." owl:sameAs "Why it matters to see, hear, approach, pay homage to, recollect and go forth following mendicants accomplished in ethics, immersion, knowledge and freedom: 'very helpful' (1.1-1.6); and living withdrawn in body and mind after hearing their teaching (1.8). Needs a pattern for what is called helpful, and the link from hearing to withdrawal is not modelled." .

"Why they are called awakening factors: they lead to awakening (bodhi) (1.5, 1.11); the list (1.6); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (1.7)." owl:sameAs "Why they are called awakening factors: they lead to awakening (bodhi) (1.5, 1.11); the list (1.6); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (1.7)." .

"Why they are called awakening factors: they lead to awakening (bodhi) (2.3, 2.6); the list (2.4); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.5)." owl:sameAs "Why they are called awakening factors: they lead to awakening (bodhi) (2.3, 2.6); the list (2.4); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.5)." .

"With a mind that has developed each factor, they penetrate and shatter the mass of greed, hate and delusion for the first time (2.2-2.4, 2.6-2.8); 'weakens' would understate 'shatter', so it waits for a better fit. Also 'abundant, expansive, limitless, and free of ill will' (2.1, 2.5)." owl:sameAs "With a mind that has developed each factor, they penetrate and shatter the mass of greed, hate and delusion for the first time (2.2-2.4, 2.6-2.8); 'weakens' would understate 'shatter', so it waits for a better fit. Also 'abundant, expansive, limitless, and free of ill will' (2.1, 2.5)." .

