"Said of all ascetics and brahmins, past, future and present, who give them up."@en owl:sameAs "Said of all ascetics and brahmins, past, future and present, who give them up."@en .

"Said of exterior factors: nothing exterior gives rise to them like good friendship."@en owl:sameAs "Said of exterior factors: nothing exterior gives rise to them like good friendship."@en .

"Said of interior factors: nothing interior gives rise to them like rational application of mind."@en owl:sameAs "Said of interior factors: nothing interior gives rise to them like rational application of mind."@en .

"Sanskrit dharma; Chinese 法. Kept as one Pali entry for v0.1."@en owl:sameAs "Sanskrit dharma; Chinese 法. Kept as one Pali entry for v0.1."@en .

"Sense of dhamma here is contested; deliberately left unassigned in v0.1."@en owl:sameAs "Sense of dhamma here is contested; deliberately left unassigned in v0.1."@en .

"Sensual desire,"@en owl:sameAs "Sensual desire,"@en .

"Some sections are modelled; dho:leftOut says what is not."@en owl:sameAs "Some sections are modelled; dho:leftOut says what is not."@en .

"Sometimes a noble disciple pays attention, applies the mind, concentrates wholeheartedly, and actively listens to the teaching. At such a time the five hindrances are absent, and the seven awakening factors are fully developed.”"@en owl:sameAs "Sometimes a noble disciple pays attention, applies the mind, concentrates wholeheartedly, and actively listens to the teaching. At such a time the five hindrances are absent, and the seven awakening factors are fully developed.”"@en .

"Source layer"@en owl:sameAs "Source layer"@en .

"Stated as a superlative: nothing else, developed like this, does so like the seven awakening factors."@en owl:sameAs "Stated as a superlative: nothing else, developed like this, does so like the seven awakening factors."@en .

"Sutta (early discourses)"@en owl:sameAs "Sutta (early discourses)"@en .

"Text"@en owl:sameAs "Text"@en .

"That’s how a mendicant who develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors slants, slopes, and inclines to extinguishment.”"@en owl:sameAs "That’s how a mendicant who develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors slants, slopes, and inclines to extinguishment.”"@en .

"That’s how the perception of a skeleton, when developed and cultivated, is very fruitful and beneficial.”"@en owl:sameAs "That’s how the perception of a skeleton, when developed and cultivated, is very fruitful and beneficial.”"@en .

"That’s how the perception of cessation, when developed and cultivated, leads to great benefit … great sanctuary from the yoke … great inspiration … great ease.”"@en owl:sameAs "That’s how the perception of cessation, when developed and cultivated, leads to great benefit … great sanctuary from the yoke … great inspiration … great ease.”"@en .

"That’s how the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated so as to lead to giving up the things that tighten the fetters."@en owl:sameAs "That’s how the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated so as to lead to giving up the things that tighten the fetters."@en .

"That’s how, when the perception of cessation is developed and cultivated, it’s very fruitful and beneficial."@en owl:sameAs "That’s how, when the perception of cessation is developed and cultivated, it’s very fruitful and beneficial."@en .

"The evidence a derived link was built from."@en owl:sameAs "The evidence a derived link was built from."@en .

"The passage(s) that state this claim."@en owl:sameAs "The passage(s) that state this claim."@en .

"The seven awakening factors should be developed for the direct knowledge, complete understanding, finishing, and giving up of these five higher fetters."@en owl:sameAs "The seven awakening factors should be developed for the direct knowledge, complete understanding, finishing, and giving up of these five higher fetters."@en .

"The seven awakening factors should be developed for the direct knowledge, complete understanding, finishing, and giving up of these five higher fetters.”"@en owl:sameAs "The seven awakening factors should be developed for the direct knowledge, complete understanding, finishing, and giving up of these five higher fetters.”"@en .

"The teaching the Buddha explained: 'the teaching is well explained by the Buddha' (svākkhāto bhagavatā dhammo)."@en owl:sameAs "The teaching the Buddha explained: 'the teaching is well explained by the Buddha' (svākkhāto bhagavatā dhammo)."@en .

"The text's own words for the relation, verbatim from the cited English (Sujato). S14 checks it occurs in a cited passage."@en owl:sameAs "The text's own words for the relation, verbatim from the cited English (Sujato). S14 checks it occurs in a cited passage."@en .

"There are the sense fields of sights, sounds, smells, tastes, touches, and ideas."@en owl:sameAs "There are the sense fields of sights, sounds, smells, tastes, touches, and ideas."@en .

"There are these seven awakening factors that are not obstacles, hindrances, or corruptions of the mind. When developed and cultivated they lead to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom."@en owl:sameAs "There are these seven awakening factors that are not obstacles, hindrances, or corruptions of the mind. When developed and cultivated they lead to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom."@en .

"There is the feature of ugliness."@en owl:sameAs "There is the feature of ugliness."@en .

"There is the heart’s release by love."@en owl:sameAs "There is the heart’s release by love."@en .

"There is the settled mind."@en owl:sameAs "There is the settled mind."@en .

"These are the five corruptions of the mind. When the mind is corrupted by these it’s not pliable, workable, or radiant. It’s brittle, and not rightly immersed in samādhi for the ending of defilements.”"@en owl:sameAs "These are the five corruptions of the mind. When the mind is corrupted by these it’s not pliable, workable, or radiant. It’s brittle, and not rightly immersed in samādhi for the ending of defilements.”"@en .

"These are the five obstacles and hindrances, corruptions of the heart that weaken wisdom."@en owl:sameAs "These are the five obstacles and hindrances, corruptions of the heart that weaken wisdom."@en .

"These five hindrances are destroyers of sight, vision, and knowledge. They block wisdom, they’re on the side of distress, and they don’t lead to extinguishment."@en owl:sameAs "These five hindrances are destroyers of sight, vision, and knowledge. They block wisdom, they’re on the side of distress, and they don’t lead to extinguishment."@en .

"These seven awakening factors are creators of vision and knowledge. They grow wisdom, they’re on the side of solace, and they lead to extinguishment."@en owl:sameAs "These seven awakening factors are creators of vision and knowledge. They grow wisdom, they’re on the side of solace, and they lead to extinguishment."@en .

"These seven awakening factors are creators of vision and knowledge. They grow wisdom, they’re on the side of solace, and they lead to extinguishment.”"@en owl:sameAs "These seven awakening factors are creators of vision and knowledge. They grow wisdom, they’re on the side of solace, and they lead to extinguishment.”"@en .

"These seven awakening factors, when developed and cultivated, lead solely to disillusionment, dispassion, cessation, peace, insight, awakening, and extinguishment.”"@en owl:sameAs "These seven awakening factors, when developed and cultivated, lead solely to disillusionment, dispassion, cessation, peace, insight, awakening, and extinguishment.”"@en .

"These seven awakening factors, when developed and cultivated, lead to going from the near shore to the far shore."@en owl:sameAs "These seven awakening factors, when developed and cultivated, lead to going from the near shore to the far shore."@en .

"They attain enlightenment early on in this very life."@en owl:sameAs "They attain enlightenment early on in this very life."@en .

"They closely watch over that mind immersed in samādhi."@en owl:sameAs "They closely watch over that mind immersed in samādhi."@en .

"They develop the awakening factor of equanimity, which relies on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripens as letting go."@en owl:sameAs "They develop the awakening factor of equanimity, which relies on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripens as letting go."@en .

"They truly know and see with a mind that has developed each awakening factor. Given in full for mindfulness, abbreviated for the others."@en owl:sameAs "They truly know and see with a mind that has developed each awakening factor. Given in full for mindfulness, abbreviated for the others."@en .

"They truly know and see with a mind that has developed the awakening factor of equanimity."@en owl:sameAs "They truly know and see with a mind that has developed the awakening factor of equanimity."@en .

"They truly know and see with a mind that has developed the awakening factor of mindfulness."@en owl:sameAs "They truly know and see with a mind that has developed the awakening factor of mindfulness."@en .

"This is how are the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated so as to lead to penetration.”"@en owl:sameAs "This is how are the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated so as to lead to penetration.”"@en .

"This is how the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated so as to lead to the cessation of craving.”"@en owl:sameAs "This is how the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated so as to lead to the cessation of craving.”"@en .

"This is the path for crushing Māra’s army.”"@en owl:sameAs "This is the path for crushing Māra’s army.”"@en .

"Timing"@en owl:sameAs "Timing"@en .

"Timing advice"@en owl:sameAs "Timing advice"@en .

"Together with bliss: 'when the body is tranquil and one feels bliss'."@en owl:sameAs "Together with bliss: 'when the body is tranquil and one feels bliss'."@en .

"Visuddhimagga IV.86"@en owl:sameAs "Visuddhimagga IV.86"@en .

"What are the five hindrances that are absent?"@en owl:sameAs "What are the five hindrances that are absent?"@en .

"What has the effect: a quality, a list, or a practice."@en owl:sameAs "What has the effect: a quality, a list, or a practice."@en .

"What seven?"@en owl:sameAs "What seven?"@en .

"What the mind is applied to, e.g. 'the feature of beauty' (subhanimitta)."@en owl:sameAs "What the mind is applied to, e.g. 'the feature of beauty' (subhanimitta)."@en .

"What the mind knows, as the sixth sense field alongside sights, sounds, smells, tastes and touches (dhammāyatana)."@en owl:sameAs "What the mind knows, as the sixth sense field alongside sights, sounds, smells, tastes and touches (dhammāyatana)."@en .

"When a mendicant has entered the first absorption, placing the mind, keeping it connected, rapture, bliss, and unification of mind are present."@en owl:sameAs "When a mendicant has entered the first absorption, placing the mind, keeping it connected, rapture, bliss, and unification of mind are present."@en .

"When a mendicant has entered the first absorption, sensual desire, ill will, dullness and drowsiness, restlessness and remorse, and doubt are given up."@en owl:sameAs "When a mendicant has entered the first absorption, sensual desire, ill will, dullness and drowsiness, restlessness and remorse, and doubt are given up."@en .

"When the body is tranquil and one feels bliss, the mind becomes immersed in samādhi."@en owl:sameAs "When the body is tranquil and one feels bliss, the mind becomes immersed in samādhi."@en .

"When the heart is overcome and mired in each hindrance, without truly knowing and seeing the escape from it. Given in full for sensual desire, abbreviated for the others."@en owl:sameAs "When the heart is overcome and mired in each hindrance, without truly knowing and seeing the escape from it. Given in full for sensual desire, abbreviated for the others."@en .

"When the mind is full of rapture, the body and mind become tranquil."@en owl:sameAs "When the mind is full of rapture, the body and mind become tranquil."@en .

"When the mind is restless, it’s the right time to develop the awakening factors of tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en owl:sameAs "When the mind is restless, it’s the right time to develop the awakening factors of tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en .

"When the mind is restless, it’s the wrong time to develop the awakening factors of investigation of principles, energy, and rapture."@en owl:sameAs "When the mind is restless, it’s the wrong time to develop the awakening factors of investigation of principles, energy, and rapture."@en .

"When the mind is sluggish, it’s the right time to develop the awakening factors of investigation of principles, energy, and rapture."@en owl:sameAs "When the mind is sluggish, it’s the right time to develop the awakening factors of investigation of principles, energy, and rapture."@en .

"When the mind is sluggish, it’s the wrong time to develop the awakening factors of tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en owl:sameAs "When the mind is sluggish, it’s the wrong time to develop the awakening factors of tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en .

"When the perception of cessation is developed and cultivated in this way you can expect one of two results:"@en owl:sameAs "When the perception of cessation is developed and cultivated in this way you can expect one of two results:"@en .

"When the perception of cessation is developed and cultivated you can expect one of two results:"@en owl:sameAs "When the perception of cessation is developed and cultivated you can expect one of two results:"@en .

"When the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated in this way these are the seven fruits and benefits they can expect.”"@en owl:sameAs "When the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated in this way these are the seven fruits and benefits they can expect.”"@en .

"When the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated in this way they can expect seven fruits and benefits."@en owl:sameAs "When the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated in this way they can expect seven fruits and benefits."@en .

"When these seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated they are noble and emancipating, and bring one who practices them to the complete ending of suffering.”"@en owl:sameAs "When these seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated they are noble and emancipating, and bring one who practices them to the complete ending of suffering.”"@en .

"When these seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated they lead to growth and progress.”"@en owl:sameAs "When these seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated they lead to growth and progress.”"@en .

"When they’re energetic, rapture not of the flesh arises."@en owl:sameAs "When they’re energetic, rapture not of the flesh arises."@en .

