7 a xsd:decimal,
        xsd:integer ;
    owl:sameAs 7 .

"The simile of the dawn (1.1)." owl:sameAs "The simile of the dawn (1.1)." .

"actively listens to the teaching" owl:sameAs "actively listens to the teaching" .

"enlightenment in this very life" owl:sameAs "enlightenment in this very life" .

"great benefit" owl:sameAs "great benefit" .

"great ease" owl:sameAs "great ease" .

"great inspiration" owl:sameAs "great inspiration" .

"great sanctuary from the yoke" owl:sameAs "great sanctuary from the yoke" .

"non-return" owl:sameAs "non-return" .

"together with the awakening factors" owl:sameAs "together with the awakening factors" .

"when you apply the mind irrationally" owl:sameAs "when you apply the mind irrationally" .

"when you apply the mind rationally" owl:sameAs "when you apply the mind rationally" .

"A mendicant accomplished in rational application of mind can expect to develop and cultivate the seven awakening factors."@en owl:sameAs "A mendicant accomplished in rational application of mind can expect to develop and cultivate the seven awakening factors."@en .

"A mendicant develops the awakening factor of equanimity, which relies on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripens as letting go. And it is abundant, expansive, limitless, and free of ill will."@en owl:sameAs "A mendicant develops the awakening factor of equanimity, which relies on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripens as letting go. And it is abundant, expansive, limitless, and free of ill will."@en .

"A mendicant develops the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en owl:sameAs "A mendicant develops the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en .

"A mendicant with good friends can expect to develop and cultivate the seven awakening factors."@en owl:sameAs "A mendicant with good friends can expect to develop and cultivate the seven awakening factors."@en .

"In the same way, for a mendicant good friendship is the forerunner and harbinger of the arising of the seven awakening factors."@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, for a mendicant good friendship is the forerunner and harbinger of the arising of the seven awakening factors."@en .

"The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity.”"@en owl:sameAs "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity.”"@en .

"There are things that are grounds for doubt."@en owl:sameAs "There are things that are grounds for doubt."@en .

"There is discontent, sloth, yawning, sleepiness after eating, and mental sluggishness."@en owl:sameAs "There is discontent, sloth, yawning, sleepiness after eating, and mental sluggishness."@en .

"There is the feature of aversion."@en owl:sameAs "There is the feature of aversion."@en .

"There is the feature of beauty."@en owl:sameAs "There is the feature of beauty."@en .

"There is the unsettled mind."@en owl:sameAs "There is the unsettled mind."@en .

"These seven awakening factors are not obstacles, hindrances, or corruptions of the mind. When developed and cultivated they lead to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom.”"@en owl:sameAs "These seven awakening factors are not obstacles, hindrances, or corruptions of the mind. When developed and cultivated they lead to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom.”"@en .

"They’re called awakening factors because they lead to awakening.”"@en owl:sameAs "They’re called awakening factors because they lead to awakening.”"@en .

"This is a cause and reason for knowing and seeing."@en owl:sameAs "This is a cause and reason for knowing and seeing."@en .

"This is a cause and reason for not knowing and not seeing."@en owl:sameAs "This is a cause and reason for not knowing and not seeing."@en .

"awakening"@en owl:sameAs "awakening"@en .

"dullness and drowsiness,"@en owl:sameAs "dullness and drowsiness,"@en .

"equanimity"@en owl:sameAs "equanimity"@en .

"ill will,"@en owl:sameAs "ill will,"@en .

"monkey mind"@en owl:sameAs "monkey mind"@en .

"restless"@en owl:sameAs "restless"@en .

"restlessness"@en owl:sameAs "restlessness"@en .

"restlessness and remorse,"@en owl:sameAs "restlessness and remorse,"@en .

"sleepy"@en owl:sameAs "sleepy"@en .

"sluggish"@en owl:sameAs "sluggish"@en .

"“Mendicant, they’re called awakening factors because they lead to awakening."@en owl:sameAs "“Mendicant, they’re called awakening factors because they lead to awakening."@en .

"“Udāyī, it’s when a mendicant develops the awakening factor of mindfulness, which relies on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripens as letting go. And it is abundant, expansive, limitless, and free of ill will."@en owl:sameAs "“Udāyī, it’s when a mendicant develops the awakening factor of mindfulness, which relies on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripens as letting go. And it is abundant, expansive, limitless, and free of ill will."@en .

"Atthi, bhikkhave, arati tandi vijambhitā bhattasammado cetaso ca līnattaṁ."@pi owl:sameAs "Atthi, bhikkhave, arati tandi vijambhitā bhattasammado cetaso ca līnattaṁ."@pi .

"Atthi, bhikkhave, cetaso avūpasamo."@pi owl:sameAs "Atthi, bhikkhave, cetaso avūpasamo."@pi .

"Atthi, bhikkhave, kāyappassaddhi cittappassaddhi."@pi owl:sameAs "Atthi, bhikkhave, kāyappassaddhi cittappassaddhi."@pi .

"Atthi, bhikkhave, paṭighanimittaṁ."@pi owl:sameAs "Atthi, bhikkhave, paṭighanimittaṁ."@pi .

"Atthi, bhikkhave, subhanimittaṁ."@pi owl:sameAs "Atthi, bhikkhave, subhanimittaṁ."@pi .

"Atthi, bhikkhave, vicikicchāṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi owl:sameAs "Atthi, bhikkhave, vicikicchāṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi .

"Kalyāṇamittassetaṁ, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—satta bojjhaṅge bhāvessati, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkarissati."@pi owl:sameAs "Kalyāṇamittassetaṁ, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—satta bojjhaṅge bhāvessati, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkarissati."@pi .

"Satisambojjhaṅgo …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo”ti."@pi owl:sameAs "Satisambojjhaṅgo …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo”ti."@pi .

"Satisambojjhaṅgo, bhikkhave, anāvaraṇo anīvaraṇo cetaso anupakkileso bhāvito bahulīkato vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattati …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo, bhikkhave, anāvaraṇo anīvaraṇo cetaso anupakkileso bhāvito bahulīkato vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattati."@pi owl:sameAs "Satisambojjhaṅgo, bhikkhave, anāvaraṇo anīvaraṇo cetaso anupakkileso bhāvito bahulīkato vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattati …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo, bhikkhave, anāvaraṇo anīvaraṇo cetaso anupakkileso bhāvito bahulīkato vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattati."@pi .

"Yonisomanasikārasampannassetaṁ, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—satta bojjhaṅge bhāvessati, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkarissati."@pi owl:sameAs "Yonisomanasikārasampannassetaṁ, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—satta bojjhaṅge bhāvessati, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkarissati."@pi .

"ayampi kho, rājakumāra, hetu, ayaṁ paccayo aññāṇāya adassanāya."@pi owl:sameAs "ayampi kho, rājakumāra, hetu, ayaṁ paccayo aññāṇāya adassanāya."@pi .

"ayampi kho, rājakumāra, hetu, ayaṁ paccayo ñāṇāya dassanāya."@pi owl:sameAs "ayampi kho, rājakumāra, hetu, ayaṁ paccayo ñāṇāya dassanāya."@pi .

"upekkhā"@pi owl:sameAs "upekkhā"@pi .

"upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ vipulaṁ mahaggataṁ appamāṇaṁ abyāpajjaṁ."@pi owl:sameAs "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ vipulaṁ mahaggataṁ appamāṇaṁ abyāpajjaṁ."@pi .

"“Idha, udāyi, bhikkhu satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ vipulaṁ mahaggataṁ appamāṇaṁ abyāpajjaṁ."@pi owl:sameAs "“Idha, udāyi, bhikkhu satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ vipulaṁ mahaggataṁ appamāṇaṁ abyāpajjaṁ."@pi .

