dho:p-sn46.24-1.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.24-1.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.24 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.24:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when you apply the mind irrationally, sensual desire,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Ayoniso, bhikkhave, manasikaroto anuppanno ceva kāmacchando uppajjati, uppanno ca kāmacchando bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya saṁvattati;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.24/en/sujato#sn46.24:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.40-1.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.40-1.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.40 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.40:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, these five hindrances are destroyers of sight, vision, and knowledge. They block wisdom, they’re on the side of distress, and they don’t lead to extinguishment."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Pañcime, bhikkhave, nīvaraṇā andhakaraṇā acakkhukaraṇā aññāṇakaraṇā paññānirodhikā vighātapakkhiyā anibbānasaṁvattanikā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.40/en/sujato#sn46.40:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.40-2.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.40-2.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.40 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.40:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "These seven awakening factors are creators of vision and knowledge. They grow wisdom, they’re on the side of solace, and they lead to extinguishment."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Sattime, bhikkhave, bojjhaṅgā cakkhukaraṇā ñāṇakaraṇā paññābuddhiyā avighātapakkhiyā nibbānasaṁvattanikā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.40/en/sujato#sn46.40:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-10.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.53-10.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:10.1" ;
    dho:textEn "When the mind is restless, it’s the wrong time to develop the awakening factors of investigation of principles, energy, and rapture."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiṁ, bhikkhave, samaye uddhataṁ cittaṁ hoti, akālo tasmiṁ samaye dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, akālo vīriyasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, akālo pītisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:10.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-10.3 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.53-10.3 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:10.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Because it’s hard to settle a restless mind with these things."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Uddhataṁ, bhikkhave, cittaṁ taṁ etehi dhammehi duvūpasamayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:10.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-13.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.53-13.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:13.1" ;
    dho:textEn "When the mind is restless, it’s the right time to develop the awakening factors of tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiñca kho, bhikkhave, samaye uddhataṁ cittaṁ hoti, kālo tasmiṁ samaye passaddhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, kālo samādhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, kālo upekkhāsambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:13.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-13.3 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.53-13.3 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:13.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Because it’s easy to settle a restless mind with these things."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Uddhataṁ, bhikkhave, cittaṁ taṁ etehi dhammehi suvūpasamayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:13.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-4.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.53-4.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:4.1" ;
    dho:textEn "When the mind is sluggish, it’s the wrong time to develop the awakening factors of tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiṁ, bhikkhave, samaye līnaṁ cittaṁ hoti, akālo tasmiṁ samaye passaddhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, akālo samādhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, akālo upekkhāsambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:4.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-4.3 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.53-4.3 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:4.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Because it’s hard to stimulate a sluggish mind with these things."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Līnaṁ, bhikkhave, cittaṁ taṁ etehi dhammehi dussamuṭṭhāpayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:4.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-7.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.53-7.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:7.1" ;
    dho:textEn "When the mind is sluggish, it’s the right time to develop the awakening factors of investigation of principles, energy, and rapture."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiñca kho, bhikkhave, samaye līnaṁ cittaṁ hoti, kālo tasmiṁ samaye dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, kālo vīriyasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, kālo pītisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:7.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-7.3 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.53-7.3 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:7.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Because it’s easy to stimulate a sluggish mind with these things."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Līnaṁ, bhikkhave, cittaṁ taṁ etehi dhammehi susamuṭṭhāpayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:7.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.1 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.1 Himavantasutta — The Himalaya"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "The seven factors developed depending on and grounded on ethics (1.4), and the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (1.6, 1.12)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "The simile of dragons growing strong on the Himalayas and reaching the ocean (1.2-1.3), and the result 'acquiring great and abundant good qualities' (1.4, 1.13). No simile pattern yet." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.1/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.12 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.12 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.12 Paṭhamasūriyūpamasutta — The Simile of the Sun (1st)"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Good friendship is the forerunner of the arising of the seven factors (1.2), and one with good friends can expect to develop them (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "The simile of the dawn as forerunner of the sunrise (1.1)." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.12/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.13 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.13 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.13 Dutiyasūriyūpamasutta — The Simile of the Sun (2nd)"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Rational application of mind is the forerunner of the arising of the seven factors (1.2), and one accomplished in it can expect to develop them (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "The simile of the dawn (1.1)." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.13/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.17 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.17 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.17 Pāraṅgamasutta — Going to the Far Shore"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Developing the seven factors leads to going from the near shore to the far shore (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "The verses (2.1-6.6): few cross to the far shore, the astute develop the bright, and those rightly developed in the awakening factors are quenched in this world." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.17/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.19 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.19 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.19 Ariyasutta — Noble"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Developing the seven factors brings one who practices them to the complete ending of suffering (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "That the factors are 'noble and emancipating' (ariyā niyyānikā) (1.1, 1.4). Needs a pattern for what a quality is called." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.19/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.20 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.20 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.20 Nibbidāsutta — Disillusionment"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Developing the seven factors leads solely to disillusionment, dispassion, cessation, peace, insight, awakening (sambodhi) and extinguishment (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.20/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.22 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.22 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.22 Bojjhaṅgadesanāsutta — A Teaching on the Awakening Factors"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Its whole teaching: the list of the seven awakening factors (1.1, 1.3, 1.4), as citations on the existing list." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.22/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.31 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.31 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.31 Paṭhamakusalasutta — Skillful (1st)"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Skillful qualities are rooted in diligence (1.1); a diligent mendicant can expect to develop the seven factors (1.2); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "'Diligence is said to be the best of them' (1.1). Needs a pattern for ranking." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.31/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.32 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.32 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.32 Dutiyakusalasutta — Skillful (2nd)"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Skillful qualities are rooted in rational application of mind (1.1); one accomplished in it can expect to develop the seven factors (1.2); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "'Rational application of mind is said to be the best of them' (1.1). Needs a pattern for ranking." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.32/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.33 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.33 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.33 Upakkilesasutta — Corruptions"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "The five corruptions of the mind as a list whose members are the same five qualities as the hindrances (2.1, 2.3, 2.4)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "The simile of the five corruptions of native gold (1.1-1.8), and what the corruptions do: the mind is not pliable, workable or radiant, is brittle, and is not rightly immersed for the ending of defilements (2.1, 2.4). No pattern yet for similes or for what a quality does." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.33/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.34 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.34 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.34 Anupakkilesasutta — Not Corruptions"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Developing the seven factors leads to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "That the factors are not obstacles, hindrances or corruptions of the mind (1.1, 1.4). Needs a pattern for what a quality is or is not." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.34/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

