    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-2.6 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.76-2.6 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:2.6" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "nirodhasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:2.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-3.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.76-3.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:3.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“The perception of cessation, when developed and cultivated, leads to great benefit … great sanctuary from the yoke … great inspiration … great ease."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Nirodhasaññā, bhikkhave, bhāvitā bahulīkatā mahato atthāya saṁvattati, mahato yogakkhemāya saṁvattati, mahato saṁvegāya saṁvattati, mahato phāsuvihārāya saṁvattati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:3.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-3.4 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.76-3.4 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:3.4" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "nirodhasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:3.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-3.5 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.76-3.5 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:3.5" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how the perception of cessation, when developed and cultivated, leads to great benefit … great sanctuary from the yoke … great inspiration … great ease.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitā kho, bhikkhave, nirodhasaññā evaṁ bahulīkatā mahato atthāya saṁvattati, mahato yogakkhemāya saṁvattati, mahato saṁvegāya saṁvattati, mahato phāsuvihārāya saṁvattatī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:3.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.21 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.21 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.21 Bodhāyasutta — To Awakening"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Why they are called awakening factors: they lead to awakening (bodhi) (2.3, 2.6); the list (2.4); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.5)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.21/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.29 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.29 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.29 Ekadhammasutta — One Thing"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Nothing else, developed like this, leads to giving up the things that tighten the fetters like the seven factors (1.1, 2.3); the list (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.2)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "What the things that tighten the fetters are: the eye, ear, nose, tongue, body and mind, where the fetters, shackles and attachments arise (3.1-3.8). Needs the six sense fields as a list and a pattern for 'X is where Y arises'." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.29/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.43 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.43 Mārasutta — About Māra"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "The seven factors are the path for crushing Māra's army (1.1, 1.5, 1.8); the list (1.7)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.43/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.5 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.5 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.5 Bhikkhusutta — A Monk"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Why they are called awakening factors: they lead to awakening (bodhi) (1.5, 1.11); the list (1.6); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (1.7)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "As they are developed the mind is freed from the defilements of sensuality, desire to be reborn and ignorance, and knows it is freed (1.8-1.10). Needs the three defilements (āsava) as a list and a pattern for release." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.5/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

5 a xsd:decimal,
        xsd:integer ;
    owl:sameAs 5 .

"It is the seven awakening factors."@en owl:sameAs "It is the seven awakening factors."@en .

"One of two results: enlightenment in this very life or, if there is residue left behind, non-return."@en owl:sameAs "One of two results: enlightenment in this very life or, if there is residue left behind, non-return."@en .

"There are qualities that are skillful and unskillful, blameworthy and blameless, inferior and superior, and those with a portion of dark or bright."@en owl:sameAs "There are qualities that are skillful and unskillful, blameworthy and blameless, inferior and superior, and those with a portion of dark or bright."@en .

"There are the elements of initiative, persistence, and exertion."@en owl:sameAs "There are the elements of initiative, persistence, and exertion."@en .

"Atthi, bhikkhave, ārambhadhātu nikkamadhātu parakkamadhātu."@pi owl:sameAs "Atthi, bhikkhave, ārambhadhātu nikkamadhātu parakkamadhātu."@pi .

"satta bojjhaṅgā."@pi owl:sameAs "satta bojjhaṅgā."@pi .

"法"@zh owl:sameAs "法"@zh .

