dho:t-sn46.24 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.24 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.24 Ayonisomanasikārasutta — Irrational Application of Mind"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Irrational application of mind: the hindrances arise and grow, the awakening factors don't arise or cease (1.1-1.6). Rational application of mind: the hindrances don't arise or are given up, the awakening factors arise and are fully developed (2.1-3.1)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.24/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.53 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.53 Aggisutta — Fire"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "The timing advice: which awakening factors it is the right or wrong time to develop when the mind is sluggish (4.1, 7.1) or restless (10.1, 13.1), the reason given for each, and 'mindfulness is always useful' (15.4)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "The setting and the challenge from wanderers of other religions (1.1-3.1); the four fire similes (5, 8, 11, 14) that illustrate the advice; the repeated statements after each simile (6, 9, 12, 15.1-15.3)." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.57 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.57 Aṭṭhikamahapphalasutta — A Skeleton"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "The perception of a skeleton is very fruitful and beneficial (1.2, 1.6), developed together with the awakening factors (1.4), with the stock formula (1.5); one of two results, enlightenment in this very life or non-return; great benefit, great sanctuary from the yoke, great inspiration and great ease." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:Opposition a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Opposition"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A one-to-one pairing of a quality against a hindrance. The suttas give the sets; the pairing comes from the commentaries."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf owl:Thing,
        dho:Opposition ;
    owl:equivalentClass dho:Opposition ;
    owl:sameAs dho:Opposition .

dho:t-sn46.37 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.37 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.37 Āvaraṇanīvaraṇasutta — Obstacles"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Both lists (1.1, 1.3-1.7; 2.1, 2.3); the hindrances weaken wisdom (1.1, 1.8); developing the awakening factors leads to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom (2.1, 2.4)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "That the hindrances are obstacles and corruptions of the heart, and the awakening factors are not (1.1, 1.8, 2.1, 2.4). Needs a pattern for what a quality is or is not." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.37/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.56 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.56 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.56 Abhayasutta — With Prince Abhaya"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "The hindrances are a cause and reason for not knowing and not seeing, when the heart is overcome by them (2.3-3.5); the awakening factors are a cause and reason for knowing and seeing (5.3-6.4); the stock formula (5.3, 6.2)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "The framing: Pūraṇa Kassapa's view that knowing and not knowing have no cause (1.4-1.13). The naming 'these are called the hindrances / awakening factors' (4.2, 7.2). Prince Abhaya's responses, including 'overcome by even a single hindrance you wouldn't truly know or see' and 'endowed with even a single awakening factor you would' (4.3-4.5, 7.3-7.6): said by the interlocutor, not taught, so not encoded (D17)." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.56/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

